Add PNG icons to the Tauri bundle so Linux builds compile

On Linux, tauri::generate_context!() uses the first .png in bundle.icon
as the default window icon and falls back to src-tauri/icons/icon.png.
The list only held .ico and .icns, so the macro panicked. List the
existing RGBA PNGs from build/sources/ (256px first, so it becomes the
window icon). The Linux bundlers read their PNG sizes from the same list.

